    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0885" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/774: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Geissler</hi>)<anchor n="41" xml:id="d574-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-27T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1928—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Please inform the Guatemalan Government of the apprehensions of the President
                    of Honduras as reported in Minister Summerlin’s <pb facs="0886" n="758"
                        xml:id="pg758"/> telegram of July 26, 4 p.m., and say that although this
                    Government assumes that some misunderstanding must exist and has entire
                    confidence in the purpose of Guatemala to maintain the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >status quo</hi>, you are directed to point out the importance of avoiding
                    the appearance of any aggressive action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d574-f1" n="41" type="source" xml:id="d574-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Minister in Honduras as No. 69.</p>
